"Status": "Active",
"EUNumber": "EU/1/12/794",
"ActiveSubstance": [
{
"LanguageCode": "EN",
"Text": "Brentuximab vedotin"
}
],
"Indication": [
{
"LanguageCode": "EN",
"Text": "Hodgkin lymphoma\r\nADCETRIS is indicated for adult patients with previously untreated CD30+ Stage III or IV Hodgkin lymphoma (HL) in combination with doxorubicin, vinblastine and dacarbazine (AVD).\r\nADCETRIS is indicated for adult patients with previously untreated CD30+ Stage IIB with risk factors, Stage III or Stage IV HL in combination with etoposide, cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin, dacarbazine, dexamethasone (BrECADD). \r\nADCETRIS is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with CD30+ HL at increased risk of relapse or progression following autologous stem cell transplant (ASCT).\r\nADCETRIS is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with relapsed or refractory CD30+ Hodgkin lymphoma (HL): \r\n1. following ASCT, or\r\n2. following at least two prior therapies when ASCT or multi agent chemotherapy is not a treatment option.\r\n\r\nSystemic anaplastic large cell lymphoma\r\nADCETRIS in combination with cyclophosphamide, doxorubicin and prednisone (CHP) is indicated for adult patients with previously untreated systemic anaplastic large cell lymphoma (sALCL).\r\nADCETRIS is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with relapsed or refractory sALCL.\r\n\r\nCutaneous T cell lymphoma \r\nADCETRIS is indicated for the treatment of adult patients with CD30+ cutaneous T cell lymphoma (CTCL) after at least 1 prior systemic therapy."
}
],
